  {
   "type": "faq",
   "items": [
    {
     "q": "What is a test automation cloud?",
     "a": "A test automation cloud runs your automated tests on hosted browsers and devices, so you do not maintain a grid."
    },
    {
     "q": "Do I need to change my tests?",
     "a": "No. You change the remote URL and capabilities; the test code stays the same."
    },
    {
     "q": "Which frameworks are supported?",
     "a": "Selenium, Playwright, Cypress, Puppeteer and Appium, plus others listed in the docs."
    },
    {
     "q": "Is there a free plan?",
     "a": "Yes. The free plan gives 100 lifetime minutes of web and mobile automation with 2 parallel sessions."
    },
    {
     "q": "How is this different from the test automation platform?",
     "a": "Automation Cloud runs your existing suites on the cloud grid. The test automation platform covers authoring tests with AI plus running them."
    }
